{"skill":{"slug":"python","displayName":"Python Coding Guidelines"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770116732964,"changelog":"Initial release providing Python coding guidelines and best practices.\n\n- Enforces PEP 8 style and modern, Pythonic patterns.\n- Requires Python 3.10+; promotes use of features from Python 3.11–3.13.\n- Includes syntax validation, unit test execution, and automatic formatting before commits.\n- Recommends `uv` for dependency management if available, with `pip` as fallback.\n- Documents clear Pythonic patterns, anti-patterns, and testing practices.\n- Provides a concise checklist for code readiness and best practices.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3864,"sha256":"8f9d2277062e2958baf8b299dbad0e30a3c90ca986da5cbb5b60e699bdf876e6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1807,"sha256":"f9ee27ae2d6c13b23c8b307d0ee5662e7cb92c12ea88f53d25df4b724afb3d3b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789030515369,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fb4c6d462da27c1bcd076517816bff5421b169bab8bf34e2f276122f4e84c09e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fb4c6d462da27c1bcd076517816bff5421b169bab8bf34e2f276122f4e84c09e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: python\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle is benign. The `SKILL.md` file provides Python coding guidelines and best practices, including standard development commands for syntax checking (`python -m py_compile`), testing (`pytest`, `unittest`), formatting (`ruff`, `black`), and dependency management (`uv`, `pip`). All instructions and commands are directly aligned with the stated purpose of enforcing coding standards and lack any indicators of malicious intent such as data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's core directives.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161074798},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789030515369},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This Python guidance skill is coherent and low risk, with only a standard caution around generic dependency installation examples.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Suggested commands such as py_compile, pytest, ruff, black, uv, and pip are proportionate to Python development tasks and are not framed as automatic background execution.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill includes generic uv/pip install examples using an unspecified package name; this is purpose-aligned for Python work but should be applied with normal package-review controls.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are limited to coding workflow guidance and do not attempt prompt override, hidden behavior, credential access, data exfiltration, or unrelated tool use.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanisms, privilege escalation, services, scheduled tasks, memory writes, or tool hijacking behavior were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill giving Python style, testing, version, dependency-management, and idiom guidance consistent with its stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before using the dependency-install snippet, confirm the exact package name and source, prefer a project virtual environment or lock file, and avoid installing packages you have not reviewed. The rest of the skill is ordinary Python coding guidance.","findings":"[T08] expected: The unpinned uv/pip dependency-install example is real, but it is disclosed, user-directed Python dependency guidance rather than hidden or unrelated behavior; treat it as a package-supply-chain caution, not a basis for Review by itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789030515369}}}}}